<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The hands-spine lane ~ the session carries the hand

The hands room covers how a person, a session and an agent act in the house. Founding bakes habits along with bytes, so the session layer lands before the bake. This lane comes first of five, because every later hands lane stands on it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">>): the scoped surfaces and holder, the hands and authorship, intent and effects, and the relay each take a session, a face and a receipt as given.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-model>>

!! The model (settled)

* ''The session carries the hand.'' A session wears the face and the vessel wears none. Every hand that reaches a vessel opens a session; the door carries and the hand authorizes. Node and browser share the model.
* ''One session, one (face, anchor)'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-27, relayed by Lares). Identity-as-relation holds for places as for faces: a session is a meeting between a face and an anchor, held by neither's registry. The anchor is the Nexus the vessel dials, or, for a vessel standing with no Nexus, that vessel's own place (its W29 place KEL prefix). The vessel's state names it, never its config: a dial pin standing means a Nexus anchor, none standing a place anchor. A proof at another anchor refuses `anchor-moved`, and a face at a second anchor opens a second session.
* ''The binding.'' A socket or port binds the owner epoch, the session id, the generation, a verified face reference (the face's proof subject) and a fixed hand profile. A copied socket refuses `unbound-session`, a wrong face `wrong-face` and a stale generation `stale-generation`.
* ''The receipt.'' A durable outcome rests under the face's proof subject plus the input digest. `requestedBy` reads as display text and leaves the digest. A later session of the same face reads the receipt; another face reads `unknown`.
* ''The working layer.'' One working document per (face, wiki, slot kind) at an address derived from the face's address secret.
* ''The switch.'' A session switches its own face in place through the five-step fence (`session:switch`); no vessel selector persists, and `persona wear` stands no more. A command names the face it acts as (`--face N`), or resolves the one face standing open; the face the unlock names (`lares vault unlock --face N`) names what the composition mounts, and no command reads it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-slices>>

!! The slices, each built with its red, its control and its known positive

# ''Contract and binding ~ BUILT.'' `SessionTable.checkBound` checks a bound message in one order (malformed, stale owner epoch, unknown session, unbound session, stale generation, wrong face, not live) and `bound` answers the five parts. The verb carries `face` through the place-verb path (`VerbPlacement`, `daemon:place-verb`, `Verb.face`), and `verbInputDigest` digests `{verb, args, face, effectKey}`. The node seat (`uds-channel.ts`) serves line-delimited session frames on a persistent socket beside the one-shot maintenance frame: `session:open` through the explicit `UdsSessionDoor` seam, `session:call`, `session:close`. The seat answers each socket's frames in arrival order, hands the worker the supplier's presenter and the face's proof subject and never the frame's `requestedBy`, and ends a session with its socket.
# ''The receipt ~ BUILT.'' `faceScopedId` namespaces a face's request ids and effect keys under a hash of its proof subject, so two faces never collide, a cancel by one never abandons another's id, and the effect index never serves one face another's effect. The outcome and the receipt fact stamp the face and the action. `session:receipt` and `session:cancel` answer a `SessionReceipt` (request id, action, face, state with `pending` and `unknown` said in words, owner epoch, boot epoch and fence, and the durable receipt); `renderSessionReceipt` prints those lines and no clock. F5: a terminal `session:result` and a terminal receipt leave only after `settleDurably` reads the daemon document's heads, flushes the Repo and names the document url, the heads and the owner epoch (`DurabilityReceipt`). The fact ring's eviction keeps the face and the action. `openLocalSession` (lares-cli) carries calls, receipt reads, cancels and close over one bound socket and sends no `requestedBy`.
# ''The working layer ~ BUILT.'' `faceWorkingDocUrl` derives the address as HMAC-SHA256 under the face's 32-byte address secret over a length-prefixed image of `FACE_WORKING_ADDRESS_DOMAIN`, the wiki id and the slot kind; the recipe's fingerprint never enters it. `resolveFaceWorkingSlot` refuses `no-address-secret`, `address-not-derived`, `secret-malformed`, `wiki-malformed` and `kind-unknown`, and zero-fills the secret it read. `materializeFaceWorkingDoc` finds or materializes the blank pinned document (`faceWorkingGenesis`) under the derived id, so two offline vessels of one face converge.
# ''The switch, the door and the retired selector ~ BUILT.'' The mesh `switchSession` runs the five steps over `SessionTable` (freeze and preflight, intent, fence, advance and commit, outcome and step live), and a commit that fails closes that session alone. The node seat serves `session:switch` with the target hint verified afresh as the preflight. The production door (`uds-session-door.ts`) reads an `h<N>` hint's anchors, its K15 atom (the presenter) and its proof at the Nexus the vessel dials (`composeFaceTarget`); it reads and writes nothing, refuses a locked face `face-locked`, any other fault `door-failed` with the detail logged, and a proof of another PersonaGroup `face-group-mismatch`. Each supply names its anchor, the Nexus its proof stands at or the vessel's own place; the socket's session records it at open, and a switch whose proof stands at another anchor refuses `anchor-moved`. A switch act rests in the vessel's own sealed `switch-acts` row and in no document: the daemon's working layer is a face bag the PersonaGroup holds admin over and syncs to the face's fleet, so a document would carry the pair of faces to every device of the outgoing face. The CLI's `openLocalSession` switches in place and refuses locally once the vessel closed its session. `persona wear` and the vessel-wide worn selector retired (`resolveFace`: named, else the one face standing open, else `FaceNotNamed`; a face's anchors never pick it); `--face N` rides cabal, host, walk, edge, persona reissue, circle, handle, realm-bag and nexus seal, and the sealed act `face.resolve` answers a command's face.
# ''The compose sites' working slot ~ BUILT'' (Lares's rulings, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28). The face's address secret mints at the face's founding, beside its atom and behind its custody (`init.ts`, the browser founding's `face-address-secret/<group>` keystore row); no read mints, the fleet-join offer reads the secret and refuses `no-address-secret` where none stands, and a face founded before the cut re-founds. A seated face's working slot is its derived address: the slot-doc resolver reads `resolveFaceWorkingSlot` by the wiki's slug through a `faceAddressSecret` port, materializes the pinned blank document (`materializeFaceWorkingDoc`), rests it and registers it once through the face door; no record names it, and the `WORKING_BINDINGS_PREFIX` record and the `working-binding` kind are gone. The port is served from main-thread custody: the node opener reads `readFaceAddressSecret` and the browser opener its keystore row, and the manifest carries the secret into the daemon worker beside the atom seed, with a face lit only. ''The floor's working document belongs to the place'' (identity-as-relation for places): with no face seated it rests in the catalog under `wikiWorkingFloorKey(slug, placeAid)`, keyed by the W29 place KEL prefix the manifest carries, never a vessel DID or a path; a floor with no place KEL refuses `no-place` by name. At the join the anon-veil lift carries each such document's tiddlers into the face's derived document for that wiki, rests it, registers it under the face, marks the place's key `lifted-from`, burns the floor document and takes the key out of the catalog last, so the place's key then names nothing and a rerun finishes a burn a stop interrupted (read G M1). The lift preflights the seated face's address secret: with none it refuses `no-address-secret` before its first step and changes nothing. ''The face's address secret follows the face'' (Lares's ruling, read G M3): the face bundle carries it in its sealed body (the carrier table's `face-address-secret` row rides whole), a restore lands those bytes through the face's founding and never mints one, a face with none refuses the cut `no-address-secret`, a body that names none refuses the restore by that name, and paper names null and lands none (custody#/the-bundle). Reds: a fresh founding's face holds its secret and resolves its working slot with no fleet join (`face-working-slot-founding.test.ts`; control: a joined vessel landing those bytes derives the same slot); a seated resolver's working slot is the derived address and a face with no secret refuses `no-address-secret` (`slot-doc-resolver.test.ts` S5); a floor working document written before any face lifts into the face's derived slot and the place's key stands empty (`anon-veil-lift.test.ts` L7; control: a face from founding never writes the place's key); a burn that faults in that lift leaves the key marked and the rerun finishes it (L9), and a face with no secret lifts nothing (L10); found on A, cut, restore on B, and both derive one working address (`face-bundle-restore.test.ts` R16; control: a second face derives another).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-seam>>

!! The adapter seam

The face supplier and the signer stand behind `UdsSessionDoor.open({ faceRef, hand })`, which answers a `UdsSessionSupply` (the `SessionFace`, the hand's profile, the presenter the worker verifies capabilities against, the facet labels). A face hint grants nothing: the supplier verifies afresh at every open. With no door the seat answers `session:open` with `no-session-door`, so a faceless vessel serves the maintenance frame alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/reds>>

!! Reds, with their controls

* A copied socket, a wrong face and a stale generation each refuse by name and reach no worker; the same-face session and a sibling session keep acting (`uds-session-socket.test.ts`, `session-contract-bound.test.ts`).
* Pipelined frames answer in order, a close queues behind the call in flight, and a vanished socket ends its own session (`uds-session-pipeline.test.ts`).
* A cross-face receipt read and cancel reveal nothing; a forged `requestedBy` attributes to the verified face; one id under two faces collides nowhere; a later same-face session recovers its receipt after the caller exits and across a restart; a terminal answer waits on the flush (`uds-session-receipts.test.ts`).
* A wrong-face working address opens nothing; the same face reopens its slot; two faces on one vessel keep separate documents; two offline vessels of one face merge (`face-working-address.test.ts`).
* A switch changes its own session alone, and a sibling of the same face keeps its generation, face and signer; the old generation signs nothing after the switch; re-wearing the same face answers unchanged and writes no act (the control); a session closed mid-preflight or mid-fence answers `session-closed` (`session-switch.test.ts`, `uds-session-switch.test.ts`).
* A switch act lands in no document, proven against a watcher that hears a known write (`uds-session-switch.test.ts`); the sealed row's ring and a malformed row (`switch-act-log.test.ts`).
* The door: a locked face's anchors refuse `face-locked`, a torn row `door-failed` with no fault text on the wire and the requestId kept, another group's proof `face-group-mismatch`, another anchor's proof `anchor-moved` (`uds-session-door.test.ts`, `uds-session-switch.test.ts`); a face with no Nexus opens at the place anchor and a command rides it, a place session ends `anchor-moved` once a pin moves the vessel, a failed re-dial ends a Nexus session the same way, and the same face opens again at the anchor the vessel stands at (`uds-session-switch.test.ts`, `place-session.test.ts`); a face row never rides the maintenance frame (`uds-session-switch.test.ts`, `store-door-session.test.ts`); a founder's session target mints no certificate (`node-face-presentation.test.ts`).
* Two faces open and a command naming none refuses, whatever face the composition mounts; one face open resolves it (`face-selector.test.ts`).
* The roll by authority: a running vessel with no face open rotates whole, its carriage anchor landed and the edge step `no-face-open` (`nexus-seal-rotate-anchor.test.ts`); the carriage row lands with no face, and the edge row refuses two open faces none named (`edge-reach-doors.test.ts`).
* Every face act rides its face: each moved act rides `session:act` on a session of the face it names, and the custody door's frame refuses it, while `petname.set` keeps the frame (`sealed-act-door.test.ts` D12, D13); an act naming another face by `handleIndex` refuses at the seat (`uds-session-switch.test.ts`).
* A rotation between a frame's check and the signature refuses `anchor-moved` at the signer (`place-session.test.ts`, `uds-session-door.test.ts`); the door's place watch keeps its KEL across a git config change and re-reads it once its bytes move (`place-rotation.test.ts`).
* Two switches over a torn switch-act row lose no intent, and the ninth set-aside refuses `switch-acts-set-aside-full` (`switch-act-log.test.ts`, `session-switch.test.ts`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/watch>>

!! Watch items and holds

* ''The `h<N>@<aid>` hint'' waits on a second Nexus: the door binds the one Nexus the vessel dials, and a hint naming a Nexus reads as malformed until a vessel dials two.
* ''The share trace.'' The face's working layer syncs to every vessel of the face's fleet, so a vessel-private act (a switch's pair of faces) rests in a sealed custody row, never in a document.
* ''The mesh `nexus-key-line` L13 load timeout'' reads red under a loaded whole-suite run and green alone; it touches nothing this lane wrote.
* ''A seat-side ledger key'' (`edge-roll-anchor`, the edge ledger key in `nexus-contract`, `edge-cosign`) acts as the face named, else the one face standing open; with two faces open and none named it refuses `FaceNotNamed` before any write. The roll anchor writes the acting face's ledger alone and answers each realm only another open face names, and each locked face, `unanchored` by name. ''The seal roll anchors by authority'' (read E H1). The carriage anchor is the place's act: `nexus-roll-anchor` and the carriage family's `nexus-roll-anchor-partial` ride the maintenance frame as place rows. Each realm edge anchor is a face's act: `nexus-roll-anchor-edge`, `-edge-open`, `-edge-partial` and `-edge-standing` ride a session as face rows, and each partial row refuses the other family by name. `nexus seal rotate` and `nexus seal anchor` resolve every face (`--face N`, else `face.resolve` with `orNone`) before the head rolls or any card reads; with no face open the edge step answers `no-face-open` by name, writes nothing, and the head lands whole.
* ''`edge kapae --quorum` keeps its face.'' The seat keys sign the act, and the acting face's edge ledger reads it: the ledger names the realm's Nexus (`actingRealmNexus`), the lease charter (`leaseCharterOf`) and the vouches the counting fold reads (`readLedgeredVouches`), and keeps the counted act (`readVesselEdgeBoard`). So two faces open with none named refuse `FaceNotNamed` there too.
* ''The place anchor and the face rows on sessions ~ BUILT'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-27). With no dial pin the door proves a face by its atom presented to its own vessel, with no Nexus admit (`supplyPlaceFace`, `PlaceSessionSigner`); the pin stands only once the vessel's own presentation composed; a session whose anchor the vessel left ends `anchor-moved`. Every store-door row that acts as a face rides a session of that face: edge-kapae, edge-partial, edge-cosign, cabal-vouch, cabal-join, cabal-face, fleet-join-offer, fleet-join-answer, the four handle rows, persona-lease, nexus-publish, raise-sign and the six intent rows. The four roll-edge rows (`nexus-roll-anchor-edge`, `-edge-open`, `-edge-partial`, `-edge-standing`) ride a session too; the carriage anchor's two rows act as the place. A row naming another face than its session's refuses `face-row-other-face`. A place anchor binds the place KEL's head: a rotation ends the place's sessions `anchor-moved`, and a read of the place that fails refuses one frame `anchor-unread`. The door reads its place through one watch (`placeReadingWatch`): the operator login reads once, so a git config change moves no anchor, and each read stats the KEL and verifies it only once its bytes moved, so a frame spawns no process. The place signer reads the same head before and after each signature, so a rotation between a frame's check and the signature refuses `anchor-moved` and drops the signer. The rows of the place keep the maintenance frame: the nexus steward rows (kapae, contract, members, cabal, release, posture, admit-take, carry-take, publish's offering read), the edge seat facts, duties and marks, persona-new, persona-kel-head and the refold. Verbs that run with no vessel open stay off sessions.
* ''The sealed acts that act as a face ~ BUILT'' (Lares's ruling, 2026-10-27). Every sealed act that signs, reads or writes as a face rides `session:act` (`SESSION_ACTS`): persona.reissue, walk.take, host.roll, crossing.sign, crossing.witness, carriage.accept, persona.guardian.enrol and persona.confirm sign under the face's key or root; handle-book.load and handle-book.save read and write the face's handle book; selves.carry and selves.clear write the face's own plane. The seat binds the session's face to the act by `face` or `handleIndex` (either naming another face refuses `face-row-other-face`); an act keyed by `face` that names none takes the session's, and the seven acts keyed by `handleIndex` alone (crossing.sign, crossing.witness, carriage.accept, persona.guardian.enrol, persona.confirm, selves.carry, selves.clear) name their face by that key, since an added `face` refuses `bad-args` at the act's reading. The seat runs it on the custody door's one chain, and the receipt names the act and the face alone (road F4); the custody door's own act frame refuses each `face-act-rides-a-session`. The cabal, edge and realm acts that take `--face` are store rows, on sessions already. Kept at the custody door, each acting as the place: face.resolve (it chooses the face, and cannot ride the session it chooses); seat.*, seal.*, cofound.* and roll-circle.* (the charter's seats); crossing.open, bind and seal (the charter's rite); petname.* and declaration.* (the place's sealed rows naming its faces; a face's plane takes a name only by selves.carry); the reads that sign no face's key (persona.roots, guardian.show, provisional, head, selves.read, walk.state, host.state, carriage.readings, crossing.state), and persona.view, which signs as a held chair (a seat key), never as a face; walk.invite and host.invite (the place's wallet); bundle.restore and bundle.import (recovery lands a face anew); and the floor's custody frames (unlock, lock, vault status, rotate, restore).
* ''A switch-act row that does not open'' moves aside unchanged to `set-aside/switch-acts.set-aside-<n>.json` beside the custody homes, and a fresh ring starts at a `reset` naming the reading and the file; the custody writer itself still refuses to overwrite bytes it cannot open, and holds no general set-aside door. Writes take turns on the row in-process, and a writer re-reads the row before it moves anything, so a fresh ring is never set aside. At most eight rows rest set aside: past the cap a switch refuses `switch-acts-set-aside-full` by name and deletes none. That refusal names the set-aside directory, and an operator alone clears it. The aborted outcome its row refuses in turn rests in the vessel's log by its act, outcome and refusal. A node-key rotation re-seals the switch-act row with every carrier-table row, so a key change never reads it `names-another-key`.
* ''The browser switch ~ OWED under W4.'' The browser compose site reads the worn face's working slot from its keystore row; switching a browser session between faces waits on W4.
* ''A `session:act` waits out its run, and a retry reads its receipt'' (read E L1-L3). An act counts as work the seat waits out on close. Its digest covers the act and the face, never an argument, so a retry under one requestId answers the receipt of the act that ran under it, whatever arguments it carries; the act runs once per id, and its answer, which rode the first socket alone, never survives a hang-up. A ledger that fails before the run answers `session-fault` (nothing ran); an act that throws once running answers `act-faulted`, and its receipt reads error; a ledger that fails to record the outcome after the run answers `act-faulted` with the receipt, and a retry under that id reads the outcome, never `pending` (read G M2). The client contract reads ''one requestId, one intent'' (session-contract#/the-hands; read G L1).
* ''The roll's edge never halves it'' (read F H1). `seal rotate` proves the acting face's session opens before any card reads (`proveFaceSession`), so a named face that cannot open one refuses the whole roll by the vessel's name with nothing written. The realm edge anchors run after the charter lands and the closing keys retire, and a retire that faults never halves the roll: the edge step and the emit still run, and `retireFault` names it (read G L2); a face that locked after the preflight leaves them `owed` by that refusal's name, and `seal anchor --edge --face N --out <partial>` opens them. The cards' seeds zero and the arming's mints retire on every path where the charter never moved. `seal anchor --from <carriage partial>` proves the reporting face's session before the carriage lands, and a face that locks after it costs the edge report alone.
* ''A provisional face opens a session'' (read F M4, measured on a real vessel, `face-bundle-restore` R15): a restored face standing provisional and a face the vessel founded each open a session at the place through the production door and mint an atom-certified signer, so `persona.confirm` and `persona.guardian.enrol` ride `session:act`.
* ''The hand profile gates no face row or act ~ OWED'' to the hands room's profile lane (read E M3). `session:call` and `session:act` check the face and the anchor, never the hand: a `watcher` or `tab` session runs a face row, or `host.roll`, as its face. That lane's profile-verb table closes it; its red: a watcher's session that calls a face row or `host.roll` refuses by its profile, and a seat's session runs it (the control).
* ''The next lane: a Keyhive provider per joined face'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-27). The daemon routes each session to its face's own provider. Its ground: K15 boots one provider at the daemon, seated for the one selected face, so a second face's session presents an atom that provider does not hold. It takes its own road row and build pair.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

